Dear Julie,

Could we open CR/14/A f.184 together at 10.00 on Wednesday 8 July? I'd like e=
ach of us to read the recto and verso without seeing the other's reading firs=
t. The old chapter passage depends rather heavily on the year I had given LA-=
042.

I've attached a one-page sheet for the desk. Before we look at that causal ar=
gument, could we record the last figure and its comparison on the recto, chec=
k the weekday, and then record the endorsement separately? We can compare not=
es afterwards. We'll open the consultation copy of both sides on the same scr=
een when we meet; it isn't attached here.

Many thanks,
Judith

